<title>HONG KONG: Lane Crawford year net jumps 91.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Lane Crawford year net jumps 91.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Earnings per A Shr (H.K. cents) 27.8	vs 14.5</p>
<p>    Earnings per B Shr (H.K. cents) 2.8	 vs 1.5</p>
<p>    Dividend A shr (H.K. cents)     13.0	vs 10.0</p>
<p>    Dividend B shr (H.K. cents)     1.3	 vs 1.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items		   28.9 gain vs nil</p>
<p>    Net				     31.4	vs 16.4</p>
<p>    Turnover				1,760.1   vs 1,790.0</p>
<p>    Company name			  Lane Crawford International</p>
<p>						Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close			   September 15-19</p>
<p>    Dividend payable		    September 25</p>
<p>NOTE - Lane Crawford International is engaged in investment holding, retailing, trading and property investment.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on disposal of certain long term investments and costs relating to closing down of store operations in Singapore and of Lane Crawford Express operations.</p>
<p>Total A share dividend for year is 30 H.K. cents (including an interim dividend of 17 cents) vs 30 cents. Total B share dividend is 2.8 cents (including an interim dividend of 1.5 cents) vs three cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368.  http://www.hk97.com</p>
</text>
